{"id":"HKF-049","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"Formulates NP-hard latency minimization over binary per-layer placement and grid-cell occupancy, solved online via centralized PPO (2-layer, 64-neuron DNN, Eq. 18) with constraint-satisfaction and latency-penalty rewards (Eqs. 13–15); p. 11 Table II training/radio cells are absent from the supplied text extract.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"III.B Problem Formulation","quote":"The proposed optimization problem depends on two decision variables ψt,i,q and δt,r,i,j"},{"page":7,"section":"III.C Reinforcement Learning","quote":"Specifically, the deep DNN model that we adopt for RL has two layers and 64 neurons for each layer"},{"page":9,"section":"III.C.5 PPO Algorithm","quote":"In order to improve the RL system performance and handle multitask operations, we chose the PPO as it can relax the complex constraints and replace them with flexible ones [42]."}],"note":"HKF-049-selected-pages.txt (orig pp. 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 11). Text-only attachment omits Table II cells on p. 11 (and Table I on p. 7); visual table values cannot be confirmed from this extract (parser limitation, not a source omission)."}
