{"id":"HKF-053","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"NO: Purely analytical single-hop numerical model assuming independent frame losses and averaged MAC access cost without collisions, A-MSDU/A-MPDU aggregation, multi-hop routing, simulation (NS-3/OMNeT++), or physical/mobile UAV testbed validation.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"Table 4","quote":"Maturity level: Analytical model, preliminary specification, without simulation validation"},{"page":8,"section":"7. Limitations of the research","quote":"First, Model (4) uses averaged medium access costs and does not account for collisions at high swarm densities"},{"page":9,"section":"7. Limitations of the research","quote":"Furthermore, the numerical estimates presented in this work were obtained for a single hop"},{"page":9,"section":"7. Limitations of the research","quote":"Validation of the model in the NS-3/OMNeT++ simulators and on a channel emulation test bench is the subject of further research within the scope of this scientific work."}],"note":"HKF-053-selected-pages.txt (orig pp. 8, 9). Text-only attachment; Table 4 and §7 explicitly establish analytical-only maturity."}
{"id":"HKF-053","kind":"technical","key":"t3_network_event_response","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Defines quorum-based graceful degradation (Phase 3: if received tensors m < q, executes degraded inference on available tensors) and binomial quorum probability Pq (Eq. 7, e.g., 0.93 for q=3 of n=6 at pf=0.9995), while explicitly leaving degraded-mode accuracy, collisions, and correlated freezes/jamming unvalidated.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"4 / Phase 3","quote":"if m < q, a degraded inference mode is executed using only the available tensors, which is consistent with the graceful degradation principle of the eCoEI architecture [13]."},{"page":6,"section":"5 / Eq. (7)","quote":"The probability of achieving a quorum q out of n = |N(i)| neighbors under independent deliveries is described by the binomial distribution"},{"page":8,"section":"7. Limitations of the research","quote":"Second, the frame delivery probabilities in (6) and (7) are assumed to be independent, which does not account for correlated freezes and intentional jamming. Third, the model does not evaluate the accuracy of inference under degraded conditions (m < q)"}],"note":"HKF-053-selected-pages.txt (orig pp. 2, 5, 6, 8). Scoped strictly to HKF-053 (SwarmNS-MAC), correcting prior cross-report mix-up."}
